## Creating a New Release

### Step 1: Create Version File
```bash
# Copy latest version as template
cp changelog/v1.02.00.md changelog/v1.XX.YY.md

# Example: For v1.3.0
cp changelog/v1.02.00.md changelog/v1.03.00.md
```

### Step 2: Update Content
- [ ] Change version number and date in header
- [ ] Write overview summary
- [ ] Document all changes in appropriate sections
- [ ] Include relevant technical details (file names, class names, counts)
- [ ] List key configuration changes
- [ ] Reference specific methods/properties when relevant

### Step 3: Update Main CHANGELOG.md
Add new entry to root `CHANGELOG.md`:
```markdown
### [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD
**Release Type**

Brief description...

**Key Changes:**
- Change 1
- Change 2

[📄 View Full Release Notes](./changelog/vX.YY.ZZ.md)
```

Update Quick Summary table:
```markdown
| Version | Date | Type | Highlights |
|---------|------|------|------------|
| [X.Y.Z](./changelog/vX.YY.ZZ.md) | YYYY-MM-DD | Type | Brief highlights |
```

### Step 4: Review Checklist
- [ ] All applicable sections completed (Added/Changed/Removed/Fixed)
- [ ] Descriptions are clear and specific
- [ ] Zero-padded filename used
- [ ] Main CHANGELOG.md updated
- [ ] No external links (internal file references are OK)
- [ ] Include relevant technical details (file names, class names, method counts)
- [ ] Focused on WHAT changed and WHY it matters

