## Version Numbering

Follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/):

- **MAJOR** (X.0.0) - Incompatible API changes, breaking changes
- **MINOR** (0.X.0) - Backward-compatible new functionality
- **PATCH** (0.0.X) - Backward-compatible bug fixes

### Examples
- `v1.00.00.md` → v1.0.0 (Initial release)
- `v1.01.00.md` → v1.1.0 (New feature, backward compatible)
- `v1.01.01.md` → v1.1.1 (Bug fix)
- `v2.00.00.md` → v2.0.0 (Breaking changes)

