## Writing Guidelines

### Be Specific
❌ BAD: "Improved performance"
✅ GOOD: "Reduced MAX_QUERY_RECORDS from 200 to 100 for 30% faster queries"

### Use Active Voice
❌ BAD: "The email template was updated"
✅ GOOD: "Updated email template to show job context"

### Include Context
❌ BAD: "Added JobContext class"
✅ GOOD: "Added JobContext class to encapsulate job metadata (SOLID Single Responsibility Principle)"

### Include Technical Context
When documenting changes, include:
- **File names** - Reference specific classes, configuration files
- **Counts** - Test method counts, property counts (when relevant to scope)
- **Class/Method names** - Specific APIs that changed
- **Configuration details** - Settings, parameters, options added

### Examples
```markdown
✅ GOOD: "Added ApexDoc to all 6 Apex classes (public and private methods)"
✅ GOOD: "Refactored 21 internal helper methods from public to private"
✅ GOOD: "Added 11 new test methods to AgentErrorMonitorServiceTest (20 → 31)"
✅ GOOD: "Prettier Configuration (.prettierrc) - 100 character print width"
❌ BAD: "Improved documentation" (too vague)
❌ BAD: "Updated some files" (not specific enough)
```

### Link to Relevant Code
When referencing specific changes, include file paths:
```markdown
- Enhanced `AgentErrorMonitorService.cls` with JobContext
- Updated `AgentErrorMonitorBatch.cls` to pass job metadata
- Added `.prettierrc` configuration file
- Modified `package.json` scripts
```

